#  tsvcomp's context indices and tunable parameters.
#
#  IDX-FORMAT.md in this directory is the specification.  idx2inc.pl turns this
#  file plus the template tsvcomp.inc into MOD/tsvcomp_h.inc (the mapping
#  objects or their folded literals, the Volumes and the table struct) and
#  MOD/tsvcomp_p.inc (the index builders).  ../mk.sh drives both builds:
#
#      ./mk.sh              tuning:   Debug 1, Const 0 -- every threshold is a
#                                     live mapping object carrying a "!MAP!"
#                                     descriptor, which is what IDX/opt.pl
#                                     scans the executable for and hill-climbs
#      ./mk.sh release      shipping: every threshold folded to a literal
#
#  Both builds must code byte-identically; ./mk.sh check is that test.
#
#  A factor whose pattern is all zeroes contributes one bucket and costs
#  nothing, which is how a variable that was tried and did not pay stays
#  visible -- and how the optimizer is given somewhere to go.  Every variable a
#  family supplies is listed in every one of its indices for that reason.

Prefix TC
Debug 1
Const 0

#  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Residue digits: 92% of the records in a stream, so this is the program.
#
#  Variables, from tsvcomp.cpp:
#    rno   which residue          pass  which cascade pass
#    band  partition, log-ish     col   position inside the partition
#    q1 q2 the two digits before it, magnitude, log-ish
#    t1    the same slot one packet ago, log-ish
#    cls   the class of this partition -- the choice of codebook
#    bkq   that codebook's `off`, log-ish: the half-width of its value range
#    zrun  zeros so far in this partition        blk  short or long block
#    pq    what the codebook makes of it: the log-odds, in 32 steps, that
#          this digit is zero, from the entry weights of the prefix the
#          vector's earlier places have already spelled (tc_prior.inc)
#    ps    what the passes before this one put at the slot, signed
#    chn   the slot's channel in a type-2 residue -- which vpos names only
#          when the book's dimension happens to be even
#    crun cm  how long the class has held, and whether it held from last packet
#
#  `cls` is the biggest single factor and the most surprising one: the class is
#  the choice of ladder and the ladder decides what a digit can be, so knowing
#  it beats knowing where in the spectrum the digit sits.  Four buckets of it
#  cost 4.65%.  `bkq` is the same thought in a form that would generalise to
#  the next file, and it measures 1.01% worse than the class number it was
#  meant to replace: two classes with the same range are still not the same
#  choice.  `col` is at zero because TSVTRANS.md measured it at +0.27% alone
#  and worse in combination, and `band` is at three buckets because the fourth
#  onwards are worth 0.05% between them once `cls` is in -- the partition had
#  been standing in for the class.
#
#  `zrun` is the cautionary tale.  It sat at pattern zero because it measures
#  at nothing on a 350 kbit/s mono residue, which is what this was tuned on;
#  on a 96 kbit/s stereo one, where two digits in three are zero, widening it
#  is worth 3% of the file.  These patterns are a joint answer over a corpus
#  that has both, and a pattern of zeroes means "not on this corpus", not
#  "never".

Index dig_a
 dig_a_rno:  rno,   1!0
 dig_a_pass: pass,  1!1111111
 dig_a_band: band, 1!111111111111111
 dig_a_col: col, 1!0100111
 dig_a_q1:   q1,    1!00000
 dig_a_q2:   q2,    1!0000
 dig_a_t1:   t1,    1!000
 dig_a_bkq: bkq, 1!0010
 dig_a_cls:  cls,   1!010100111000000
 dig_a_zrun: zrun,  1!0000
 dig_a_blk:  blk,   1!1
 dig_a_vpos: vpos,  1!0
 dig_a_q1s:  q1s,  -6!0000000000000
 dig_a_q2s:  q2s,  -6!0000000000000
 dig_a_t1s:  t1s,  -6!0000000000000
 dig_a_t2:   t2,   1!000
 dig_a_n1:   n1,   1!000
 dig_a_w1:   w1,   1!000
 dig_a_p0:   p0,   1!000
 dig_a_p0s: p0s, -6!0100000000000
 dig_a_pn:   pn,   1!000
 dig_a_ax: ax, 1!000000100000
 dig_a_pq: pq, 1!00000000100000000000000010000000
 dig_a_ps:   ps,   -6!0000000000000
 dig_a_chn: chn, 1!1010101
 dig_a_crun: crun,  1!000000000
 dig_a_cm:   cm,    1!0

